    },
    "message": "Fix LLM runtime fallbacks that made API runs match offline\n\n- Bound support-priority requests (support-priority-v2): ask only for\n  requesters with stress >= 0.65 and at most 4 per simulated day; others keep\n  the rule priority 0 without a provider call. Previously every pending\n  request asked, so ~256 calls/day exhausted the 10-call cap at minute 0 and\n  social proposals were never reached. The limits are recorded as\n  ASM-SUPPORT-PRIORITY-LIMITS-V1 and counted in support_priority_runtime_v1.\n  Histories that contain support-priority-v1 calls keep v1 so recorded\n  responses still replay exactly; offline runs are unchanged.\n- Tell the model to keep rationale to 80 characters. Live v1 replies often\n  exceeded the 160-character schema limit and were rejected.\n- Open a fresh CLI usage account per prepare/run (cli-prepare-*, cli-run-*)\n  instead of the shared cli-default, whose immutable limits silenced every\n  later run once exhausted. The campaign ledger still bounds total spend.\n- Serialize response tape citations as lists. The tuple form made Project\n  storage reject every Checkpoint holding an accepted response as\n  \"sensitive data\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
